cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its code, please cite the manuscript."
title: "When Objects Overshadow Materials: Benchmarking and Adapting Multimodal Large Language Models for Construction and Demolition Waste Auditing"
authors:
  - family-names: Cao
    given-names: Jin Xin
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Shi Yang
year: 2026
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/IMUJason/cdw-vqa-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  CDW-VQA is a visual question answering benchmark for construction and demolition waste auditing,
  built from public segmentation datasets, with a scene-level suite, an instance-level four-arm suite,
  two human reference cohorts, two-level material scoring, and a diagnosis of what language-side
  instruction tuning repairs.
